          <div class="inner_column text_header">
            <h1>nest R&amp;D</h1>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="inner_column profile_content">
          <div class="columns">
            <div class="column profile_column">
              <center>
                <div class="user_links" style="background-color: #191a19; border-radius: 10px;">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
                  <span class="link_group for_nil"><a rel="me" href="https://nestrd.github.io/">home</a>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;|&nbsp;</span>
                  &nbsp;&nbsp; <span class="link_group for_nil"><a rel="me" href="https://nest.itch.io/">itch.io</a>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;|&nbsp;</span>
                  &nbsp;&nbsp; <span class="link_group for_nil"><a rel="me" href="https://twitter.com/liswifi">twitter</a>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
                    |&nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;</span> <span class="link_group for_nil"><a
                      rel="me" href="https://lismiller.bandcamp.com/">bandcamp</a>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;|</span>
                  &nbsp; &nbsp; <span class="link_group for_nil"><a rel="me" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/nestrd/">linkedin</a>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;|</span>
                  &nbsp;&nbsp; <span class="link_group for_nil"><a rel="me" href="ToriMillerResume.pdf">résumé</a>&nbsp;&nbsp;</span>
                </div>
              </center>
            </div>
            <div class="column game_column" style="background-color: #191a19; padding-left: 10px; padding-right: 10px; padding-top: 10px; padding-bottom: 12px; border-radius: 10px;">
              <div class="game_grid_widget user_game_grid"> </div>
              <div class="game_cell_data">
                <div class="game_title"> <span class="game_text" data-action="game_grid"
                    style="font-size: 16pt; text-shadow: 0px 0px 2px black;">Tori
                    'Lis' Miller, Technical Game Designer &amp; Researcher </span>
                </div>
                <div class="game_text" style="text-shadow: 0px 0px 2px black;">
                  <p style="box-sizing: border-box; margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 1rem; color: rgb(239, 232, 232); font-family: Lato, Lato, LatoExtended, sans-serif; font-size: 16px; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; white-space: normal; background-color: rgb(25, 26, 25); text-decoration-thickness: initial; text-decoration-style: initial; text-decoration-color: initial;">Hi
                    there! My name is Tori, though I go by Lis in some spaces,
                    and I'm a technical designer in the South Midlands, UK.
                    Recently, I finished work on the highly anticipated<span>&nbsp;</span><a
                      href="https://www.fablethegame.com" style="box-sizing: border-box; color: rgb(215, 168, 122); text-decoration: none; background-color: transparent;">Fable
                      (Xbox/Playground Games)</a>, where I worked within the
                    quest team to create the main quest-line and related
                    gameplay features. Before my time on Fable, I completed an
                    MSc with First-Class Honours in Computer Game Design at the
                    University of Staffordshire, in which I focused on game AI,
                    gameplay systems design, and narrative-driven games. My main
                    interests in game development are in player mechanics for
                    action-adventure games, designing puzzles, telling stories
                    thoughtfully via gameplay mechanics, and building deep and
                    scalable gameplay systems.</p>
                  <p style="box-sizing: border-box; margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 1rem; color: rgb(239, 232, 232); font-family: Lato, Lato, LatoExtended, sans-serif; font-size: 16px; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; white-space: normal; background-color: rgb(25, 26, 25); text-decoration-thickness: initial; text-decoration-style: initial; text-decoration-color: initial;">Aside
                    from my professional output, I have also presented talks on
                    game development at<span>&nbsp;</span><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=a41i5fSkIis"
                      style="box-sizing: border-box; color: rgb(215, 168, 122); text-decoration: none; background-color: transparent;">Snappy
                      Gurus Career Week</a>, as well as a postmortem of the<span>&nbsp;</span><a
                      href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1rOOUpv7mLg" style="box-sizing: border-box; color: rgb(215, 168, 122); text-decoration: none; background-color: transparent;">virtual
                      tour project 'Staffsverse'</a><span>&nbsp;</span>for the
                    University of Staffordshire, and the Interactive Games
                    Post-Graduate Research Conference where I discussed the
                    development and research of my<span>&nbsp;</span><a href="https://x.com/investigatedot/status/1811784368450384007"
                      style="box-sizing: border-box; color: rgb(215, 168, 122); text-decoration: none; background-color: transparent;">dynamic
                      horror system</a>. Additionally, I have experience working
                    with<span>&nbsp;</span><a href="https://nest.itch.io/joycon-motion-adventure-framework"
                      style="box-sizing: border-box; color: rgb(215, 168, 122); text-decoration: none; background-color: transparent;">motion
                      controls</a><span>&nbsp;</span>(Nintendo Joy-Con &amp;
                    Wii), and<span>&nbsp;</span><a href="https://github.com/nestrd/Companion-PLUS/tree/main"
                      style="box-sizing: border-box; color: rgb(215, 168, 122); text-decoration: none; background-color: transparent;">Augmented
                      Reality games</a>, due to my love for innovative games. To
                    relax outside of my time active in game development, I also
                    record my own<span>&nbsp;</span><a href="https://lismiller.bandcamp.com/album/projects-pt1-2022"
                      style="box-sizing: border-box; color: rgb(215, 168, 122); text-decoration: none; background-color: transparent;">music</a><span>&nbsp;</span>and
                    spend time outdoors doing photography.</p>
                  <p style="box-sizing: border-box; margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 1rem; color: rgb(239, 232, 232); font-family: Lato, Lato, LatoExtended, sans-serif; font-size: 16px; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; white-space: normal; background-color: rgb(25, 26, 25); text-decoration-thickness: initial; text-decoration-style: initial; text-decoration-color: initial;">Currently,
                    I am seeking in-person (between the London and Birmingham
                    areas) or remote (UK/EU) work in technical design, gameplay
                    design or gameplay programming roles. During my current
                    employment gap, I am working as a solo developer on a
                    narrative puzzle game hobby project, which I am journaling
                    the development of over at<span>&nbsp;</span><a href="https://x.com/liswifi"
                      style="box-sizing: border-box; color: rgb(215, 168, 122); text-decoration: none; background-color: transparent;">Twitter</a>.</p>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <br>
